Recovery/convalescent phase

In dengue fever, patients moving from the febrile phase to the recovery phase show clinical improvement. The following are the features of recovery:





improving general conditions and appetite; bradycardia;

convalescent rash – characterized as confluent petechial rash with scattering white halo on extremities, itching, especially on palms and soles;

diuresis; and

increasing platelet count.



